_atom_sites_footnote.text   
;THREE RESIDUES IN THE SEQUENCE STUDIED ARE CYTOSINES THAT ARE PROTONATED AT THE N3 POSITION. THESE RESIDUES DIFFER FROM "NORMAL" CYTOSINES IN THAT THEY HAVE A PROTON ATTACHED TO THE N3 NITROGEN. IT SHOULD BE NOTED THAT THIS IS NOT A PERMANENT MODIFICATION BUT RATHER A CONSEQUENCE OF THE CONDITIONS UNDER WHICH THE SEQUENCE WAS STUDIED. THESE N3-PROTONATED CYTOSINE RESIDUES HAVE BEEN ASSIGNED THE RESIDUE NAME C IN THE ENTRY AND ATOM H3 HAS BEEN FOOTNOTED.
;
